 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#frequently-asked-questions-about-claude-skills"&gt;Frequently Asked Questions About Claude Skills&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href="#automate-marketing-tasks-with-claude-skills"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#automate-marketing-tasks-with-claude-skills"&gt;Automate marketing tasks with Claude skills.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;What Claude Skills Are and Who Should Build Them&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;A Claude skill is a self-contained folder that teaches Claude how to perform a specific task and loads automatically when a matching task comes up. Each skill folder contains a required SKILL.md file and may also include references, assets, or scripts. The skill loads only when the task matches the skill capability. Claude skills are available on all plans.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hubfs/blogbot/how-to-create-claude-skills-what-your-team-actually-needs-2-20261023-2127745.webp" style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 650px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;" alt="Claude skills landing page"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://claude.com/skills"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12px;"&gt;Source&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Skills can be made by chatting with Claude in plain language — no coding required. Users just describe the workflow and save it as a new Claude skill. Marketers and RevOps professionals can use a Claude skill creator without a technical background.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Users just describe the workflow and save it as a new Claude skill. For example, a content marketer may use their brand guidelines to build an editing skill. Or, a learning and development expert may build a skill to help write SOPs.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hubfs/blogbot/how-to-create-claude-skills-what-your-team-actually-needs-3-20261023-4331863.webp" style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 650px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;" alt="Coders and Non-coders can build and customize their own Claude skills"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://claude.ai/new%23customize/skills/yours"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12px;"&gt;Source&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Teams need a developer when a skill bundles Python, Bash, or Node.js scripts, which require debugging. Similarly, if Claude cannot access a system or call a proprietary API, developers need to configure, host, and wire up the connection with authentication and permissions.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;How do Claude skills work?&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Claude skills rely on a progressive disclosure mechanism. Instead of stuffing skill details into the context window up front, Claude loads a skill’s contents in layers, only as much as the task requires. There are three levels at which Claude skills work:&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Level 1 (metadata, always loaded).&lt;/strong&gt; At the start of a session, Claude reads only the name (64 characters maximum) and description (1024 characters maximum) of every installed skill. Users can install multiple skills without paying a large ongoing context cost.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Level 2 (markdown body, loaded on trigger):&lt;/strong&gt; Once Claude decides a skill matches the current request, it loads the full step-by-step instructions by accessing the skill.md file.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Level 3 (bundled files/scripts, loaded when referenced):&lt;/strong&gt; Claude reads the supporting Reference.md files, templates, or executable code from the skill directory only when the instructions actually call for them. So, even a large skill stays light until a specific branch of the work needs that material.&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hubfs/blogbot/how-to-create-claude-skills-what-your-team-actually-needs-4-20261023-4547361.webp" style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 650px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;" alt="Window showing how to create Claude skills"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://claude.ai/new%23customize/skills/yours"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12px;"&gt;Source&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The only text Claude sees when deciding whether to load a particular skill is the skill description. A vague or overlapping skill description causes trigger confusion. Since the description is the trigger, write it to match intent, and the rest of the skill only ever loads when it should.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;For example, &lt;a href="https://support.claude.com/en/articles/12512198-how-to-create-custom-skills%23h_db275d1972"&gt;Claude’s official documentation&lt;/a&gt; offers this example: &lt;em&gt;“Apply Acme Corp brand guidelines to presentations and documents, including official colors, fonts, and logo usage.”&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;How to Create Claude Skills Withou...

&lt;p&gt;Profound and Bluefish AI both help marketing teams measure how brands appear in AI-generated answers, including visibility, citations, and competitive presence. Profound and Bluefish AI differ in their approach to engine coverage, prompt controls, data capture, reporting, and how insights translate into action.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
