&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;What are LLM visibility tools?&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;LLM visibility tools measure whether and how a brand appears in AI-generated answers across answer engines such as ChatGPT, Gemini, Perplexity, and Google AI Overviews. Unlike traditional SEO rank tracking, these tools measure patterns across repeated AI responses rather than one fixed position. They typically record:&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Whether a brand is mentioned or cited&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;How the brand is described&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Which competitors appear for the same prompts&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;How results change across engines and over time&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;How do LLM visibility tools work?&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;LLM visibility tools start with prompts modeled on questions people might ask while researching a category, problem, or product. The tool runs those prompts through its supported answer engines and records the responses.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;A single manual check can show what an answer engine says at that moment, but reliable answer engine tracking requires repeatable prompts across multiple engines and time periods. The same prompt can return different answers between runs, so ongoing tracking tools repeat those checks on a schedule and measure patterns over time.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;LLM visibility tools typically measure brand mentions, citations, sentiment, share of voice, competitor presence, and placement frequency depending on the platform. A mention within an AI tool looks like the following example:&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hubfs/blogbot/llm-visibility-tools-1-20261005-2689053.webp" style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 650px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;" alt="AI visibility tools, ChatGPT answer listing five CRM brands without clickable citations"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The answer mentions five CRM brands, but none has a clickable citation. A citation includes a clickable link, and it looks like this:&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hubfs/blogbot/llm-visibility-tools-2-20261005-8545158.webp" style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 650px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;" alt="LLM visibility tools, Google AI Overviews answer showing linked source cards and citations"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;A citation points readers to a source that was used or referenced in the generated answer. Citations can drive direct visits to websites, while unlinked mentions still contribute to a brand’s overall visibility.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Within the visibility tracking section, these tools measure two key dimensions: visibility tracking shows whether and how often a brand appears in generated answers, while citation analysis shows which domains, URLs, and content types appear as sources.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;What to Look For in LLM Visibility Tools&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Marketers can compare LLM visibility tools across six practical criteria: engine coverage, prompt management, citation insights, competitor views, reporting, and workflow fit.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engine Coverage&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Engine coverage refers to which answer engines a tool tracks and whether those engines match the places a brand wants to monitor. Coverage can vary by plan, so marketers should compare what is included at the entry tier with what requires an upgrade.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;For example, &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/aeo"&gt;HubSpot AEO&lt;/a&gt; tracks ChatGPT, Gemini, and Perplexity. Profound tracks ChatGPT on its Starter tier, three answer engines on the Growth tier, and up to nine on the Enterprise tier.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prompt Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Prompt management covers how teams add, edit, organize, and refresh the questions they track. Some products suggest prompts automatically, while others rely more heavily on manual setup.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Teams should also check what informs those prompt suggestions. Standalone HubSpot AEO uses company, competitor, and industry context, while &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/marketing/aeo"&gt;AEO in Marketing Hub&lt;/a&gt; Professional and Enterprise can use CRM data to surface prompts relevant to actual buyers.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Citation Insights&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Citation analysis shows which domains, URLs, and content types appear as sources in AI-generated answers. That information can help marketers identify owned-content gaps, third-party publications worth monitoring or pitching, and competitors whose content appears frequently.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Competitor Views&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Competitor reporting shows how a brand’s visibility compares with other companies for the same or related prompts. Depending on the tool, comparisons can include share of ...

&lt;p&gt;If you’re comparing Profound vs. Scrunch, the buying decision usually comes down to where your AEO workflow stalls, not which tool tracks more answer engines. Both Profound and Scrunch measure how AI answers cite your brand, but they’re built for different jobs: Profound leans toward market analysis and content creation, while Scrunch leans toward technical optimization and task handoff.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class="cta_button" href="https://www.hubspot.com/cs/ci/?pg=9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18&amp;amp;pid=53&amp;amp;ecid=&amp;amp;hseid=&amp;amp;hsic="&gt;&lt;img class="hs-cta-img " style="height: auto !important; width: auto !important; max-width: 100% !important;border-width: 0px; /*hs-extra-styles*/; margin: 0 auto; display: block; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px" alt="Get Started with HubSpot's AEO Tool" height="58" width="335" src="https://no-cache.hubspot.com/cta/default/53/9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18.png" align="middle"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;This comparison article will walk you through the criteria that make them different: how many answer engines each plan covers, prompt capacity, reporting depth, technical optimization, bot-traffic tracking, actionability, agency and international fit, and pricing. Each section names which tool leads and why, so you can find the best fit for your team.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;I’ll also include &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/aeo"&gt;HubSpot AEO&lt;/a&gt; as a third option, since teams already running their content and CRM in one place often want visibility data that connects to their publishing workflow. I’ll compare Profound vs. Scrunch first, then explain where a CRM-connected tool makes sense and where it doesn’t.&lt;/p&gt; 
