&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;What is an AI agent?&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;An AI agent is software that uses an AI model to work toward a goal &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/autonomous-agents"&gt;&lt;em&gt;autonomously&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, or without human input. Agents can choose among approved tools, review the results, and decide what to do next until they finish the task or reach a set limit.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Agents need pre-defined goals or functions. For a marketing team, that could be to review a campaign’s performance and recommend optimizations. The agent would need to examine channel metrics, compare results with the campaign objective, identify likely causes, and explain the recommended change.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Looking to build your first agent? HubSpot users now have access to a no-code AI agent builder. Marketers can describe the automation they want to create, and &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/artificial-intelligence/ai-agents"&gt;Agent Builder&lt;/a&gt; will do the rest.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;AI Agent vs. Chatbot vs. Rules-Based Automation: Explaining the Difference&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/service/ai-agent-vs-chatbot"&gt;Agents, chatbots&lt;/a&gt;, and workflows have different problem-solving capabilities and serve different functions:&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Chatbots respond to queries or conversations, answering questions that the user inputs.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Agents are able to make decisions on their own and problem-solve independently.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Rule-based automations perform a predefined task based on a set trigger. For example, if a buyer changes deal stages, an email may be sent with a discount code.&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Agents, chatbots, and automations can also work together. A chatbot, for example, can act as the conversation window for an agent, as well as a predefined workflow can also include an agentic step&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;The Four Building Blocks of an AI Agent&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;An effective custom AI agent needs a repeatable job, relevant data, a clear starting point, and a measurable result, as defined by Elle Oshiro, a professor at &lt;a href="https://academy.hubspot.com/"&gt;HubSpot Academy&lt;/a&gt;. These four building blocks help marketers turn an idea into a workflow they can put to use.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h4&gt;1. Repeatable Work&lt;/h4&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;AI agents excel at regular tasks that need to be performed consistently. For example, a marketing team might review lost deals each month to identify buyer concerns. Even though each deal contains different evidence, the agent’s job stays the same: examine the concern, check existing assets, and recommend a next step.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;That said, choose a task that the team can describe clearly and expects to perform&lt;em&gt; over and over&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h4&gt;2. Data Already in Your CRM&lt;/h4&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;AI agent development relies on high-quality training data. CRM data gives the AI context it can use to make decisions. Relevant information might include deal properties, company details, sales notes, and recorded customer conversations.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Before building an agent, check whether the necessary information exists, is current, and is accessible to the agent.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h4&gt;3. A Trigger That Fires Under the Right Conditions&lt;/h4&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;A trigger determines when the agent starts its work. It could be a manual request, a schedule, or a change to a CRM record. With HubSpot, marketers and sales ops can use any of these options through &lt;a href="https://knowledge.hubspot.com/workflows/select-workflow-triggers-in-agent-hub"&gt;Agent Hub workflow triggers&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h4&gt;4. A Clearly Defined, Measurable Outcome&lt;/h4&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Define what the agent must deliver, what a correct result looks like, and how the team will measure success. For a campaign review, the output could be a report that flags underperforming channels and recommends one change to test. Each recommendation should cite the relevant metrics, explain the rationale, and acknowledge data gaps.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Is an AI agent the right fit for your workflow?&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;AI agents are worth a closer look when a task is repeatable, tedious, and requires interpreting information&lt;em&gt; and&lt;/em&gt; deciding what to do next. If all you need is a summary of text or data analysis you paste into a chat, a single AI prompt may do the job. Even Anthropic &lt;a href="https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/building-effective-agents"&gt;recommends&lt;/a&gt; starting with the simplest approach that meets the need, since agents can add cost and delay.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Three questions to ask before you build:&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Where does the task requ...

&lt;p&gt;Companies without the internal resources or budget to build a dedicated search department still need to know what options exist for running AEO without a large team. Answer Engine Optimization is no longer optional for companies that rely on search to generate leads and revenue. AI Overviews now appear at the top of search results before a single organic listing — and sometimes above paid ads.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class="cta_button" href="https://www.hubspot.com/cs/ci/?pg=9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18&amp;amp;pid=53&amp;amp;ecid=&amp;amp;hseid=&amp;amp;hsic="&gt;&lt;img class="hs-cta-img " style="height: auto !important; width: auto !important; max-width: 100% !important;border-width: 0px; /*hs-extra-styles*/; margin: 0 auto; display: block; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px" alt="Get Started with HubSpot's AEO Tool" height="58" width="335" src="https://no-cache.hubspot.com/cta/default/53/9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18.png" align="middle"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Three paths exist for running AEO without a large team. The first is a DIY workflow built around free or low-cost tools. The second is a complete software solution like &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/aeo"&gt;HubSpot AEO&lt;/a&gt; that centralizes tracking and recommendations. The third is agency support for teams that want the work handled externally.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The right path depends on how much time the team can dedicate each week, what budget is available, and how consistently measurement can be turned into action. This article covers each path, walks through a minimum viable workflow for getting started, and provides starter prompts for building a repeatable tracking system.&lt;/p&gt; 
